// espeak-ng voice variant: a gender-neutral controller voice.
//
// Installed into espeak-ng's voices/!v directory by build-phrase-bank.py and
// used as "en+rt-neutral". Chosen by measuring fundamental frequency rather
// than by ear: the shipped variants all sit clearly to one side — the male
// ones around 90-110 Hz, the female ones around 195 Hz — with none in the
// ambiguous band between.
//
// Two things make this one neutral:
//
//   pitch    165 205 measures a median F0 of ~171 Hz across a sample of real
//            bank tokens, the centre of the androgynous range between typical
//            male (~110 Hz) and typical female (~210 Hz).
//
//   formant  left at 100% across the board. Perceived gender follows formant
//            positions as much as pitch, and the shipped variants shift them:
//            the male ones scale to ~96%, the female ones to 105-120% while
//            also adding breath, roughness and echo. Leaving them unscaled is
//            the actual midpoint rather than a lean in either direction.
//
// The pitch numbers are tuned against single tokens, not sentences. Every clip
// in the bank is rendered on its own, so each one gets espeak's utterance-final
// falling intonation; the same setting measures roughly 20 Hz higher on a full
// sentence. Re-tune against tokens, not prose, or the bank comes out flat.
//
// Note the bank is highpassed at 300 Hz afterwards, which removes the
// fundamental itself. The pitch still reads correctly through the harmonics —
// the missing-fundamental effect, and exactly what real radio and telephone
// audio does.

language variant
name rt-neutral
gender unknown

pitch 165 205

formant 0 100 100 100
formant 1 100 100 100
formant 2 100 100 100
formant 3 100 100 100
formant 4 100 100 100
formant 5 100 100 100
formant 6 100 100 100
formant 7 100 100 100
formant 8 100 100 100

consonants 100
